    "authors": [
      {
        "affiliation": "DTTR Users' Ad Hoc Group CBS Operations and Engineering New York, New York",
        "bio": "William C. Nicholls, Director, Systems Development, Engineering and Development Department, CBS, graduated from Purdue University with a BSEE. After working at two CBS affiliated stations, he joined CBS and came to New York in 1966. Since then, he has worked on many projects for the Engineering and Development Department. Mr. Nicholls has served on many SMPTE committees, including the Video Recording and Reproduction Technology Committee, the Digital Television Tape Recording Working Group, and all the DTTR Ad Hoc Groups. In addition, he is a member of the EIA NABTS Teletext Ad Hoc Group, as well as EBU Sub Group G-2 (Television Tape Recoding) and EBU Specialist Group MAGNUM (Component Digital VTR). He acts as liaison between VRRT and G-2, and between DTTR and MAGNUM. The holder of a patent for Dual Frequency Time Code, Mr. Nicholls has given papers at SMPTE Technical Conferences and the Montreux Television Symposium.",
        "name": "William C. Nicholls"
      }
    ],
